From c94077ffd65bf09c68f7654196fdca0ea1886668 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 15:53:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 63/64] Audio: the minimum window starts early by its expected
 render time, so the buffer keeps its reserve

The minimum window (ffdebd79) waited until 32 samples were due and rendered about twice that. The render's own time
came on top: at tests/sdload S4's 38 % load a render of 60 samples ended with 55 due, and one where voices started
with 78 (79 of the output buffer's 128 samples gone: the worst DMA gap, v16 45).

Now it renders its 60 samples (or twice what's due less 6, if more) once 32 less the expected render time are due
(the window at the load measured, windowLoadPermille; 8 at the latest), so that the render ends with about 32 due
whatever the load. Same windows, so the same CPU; the samples rendered ahead after a render are ~28 at any load (before
28 less the render time).

tests/sdload (the CPU at 400 MHz, 1 instruction per cycle; device = + 60 ns per SDRAM line touched; UI = the pads,
sidebar and OLED redrawn every 10 ms by the firmware's own functions), v16 / v17 before / now:
  S2 idle     calls/s 7,126 / 2,945 / 2,960, samples per render 6.2 / 60 / 60, monitor 90.2 / 11.7 / 11.6 %,
              device 182 / 19.1 / 19.1 %, worst gap 19 / 49 / 46 (with UI 22 / 49 / 46)
  S4 typical  calls/s 5,309 / 2,593 / 3,217, samples per render 8.4 / 60.2 / 59.9, monitor 92.7 / 38.6 / 38.3 %,
              device 97.7 / 39.6 / 39.5 %, worst gap 45 / 79 / 65 (with UI 50 / 81 / 65), culls 37 / 0 / 0
  clock       (S4's song on an external MIDI clock, typical card) worst gap 55 / 78 / 59, with UI 59 / 78 / 59
No underruns. The one gap over 64 left (65) is when playback starts: the first renders with voices, at the load
measured while idle.

